From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: run the pool warmer's censuses about every five
 minutes

The pool warmer's ~2 s cycle ran the slot probe and the window
inventories every 15th cycle and the physical-map walk over every
region every 5th. In a Portal 2 chamber the walk covers about 78,000
regions. One took a P-core for 154 ms inside a 596 ms chamber hitch,
while the game thread all but stopped.

Run both censuses on their early cycles (1 and 2), as before, and then
every 150th cycle. The page warming, the pool-rot sweep, the zone check
and the per-cycle footprint line are unchanged.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-04-portal2-gameplay.md
Offered-upstream: no; diagnostics of the iOS port's pool
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index b35cd20..e1da28e 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -655,6 +655,14 @@ static void ios_window_inventory( const char *why, unsigned long long lo_arg, un
 extern unsigned long long ios_last_footprint_mb;
 extern int ios_fast_footprint;
 
+/* Playport: the warmer's full censuses -- the slot probe and window
+ * inventories, and the physical-map walk over every region (77,684 in a Portal
+ * 2 chamber) -- ran every 15th and 5th ~2 s cycle. One took a P-core for
+ * 154 ms while the game thread all but stopped, inside a 596 ms chamber hitch.
+ * They now run once early (cycles 1 and 2) and then about every five minutes;
+ * the page warming and the cheap per-cycle lines are unchanged. */
+#define IOS_WARMER_CENSUS_CYCLES 150
+
 static void *ios_pool_warmer_thread( void *arg )
 {
     unsigned cycle = 0;
@@ -795,7 +803,7 @@ static void *ios_pool_warmer_thread( void *arg )
                     dprintf(2, "[pool-rot] clean: %lu .text pages sampled across %u mappings (cycle=%u)\n",
                             (unsigned long)checked, ios_jit_mapping_count, cycle);
             }
-            if (cycle == 1 || (cycle % 15) == 0)
+            if (cycle == 1 || (cycle % IOS_WARMER_CENSUS_CYCLES) == 0)
             {
                 /* ml469 (wall #79): one-shot proof of whether TCP loopback
                  * works at all under this port — the webhelper's transport
@@ -938,9 +946,9 @@ static void *ios_pool_warmer_thread( void *arg )
              * vs FEX lookup caches vs CEF heap. Walk the address space and
              * charge private-dirty+swapped pages to each region; the base
              * addresses identify the owner offline (pool = RX base, FEX bands,
-             * PA pools, guest heap). Every 5th cycle plus cycle 2, because the
-             * walk is tens of thousands of kernel calls. */
-            if (cycle == 2 || (cycle % 5) == 0)
+             * PA pools, guest heap). Cycle 2, then every IOS_WARMER_CENSUS_CYCLES
+             * cycles, because the walk is tens of thousands of kernel calls. */
+            if (cycle == 2 || (cycle % IOS_WARMER_CENSUS_CYCLES) == 0)
             {
                 struct { unsigned long long base, size, dirty, res, swap; unsigned tag; } top[12];
                 unsigned long long dirty_by_tag[256];
-- 
